; cadence-from-masked-steps-band.fk — tempo out of a sensor that masks its values.
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk observe/cadence-from-masked-steps.fk
;
; Fixtures are WITNESSED, not invented: six step_counter events read over USB from
; R5CW20DK17A on 2026-07-22 at 16:40:33-36, every one of them `[value masked]`, and an
; earlier walk at 15:20 whose long pauses split it into unusable pieces.
;
; Verdict 127 when, on Go / Rust / TypeScript / fkwu:
;     1  six timestamps yield five intervals
;     2  those intervals sum to 3057 ms
;     4  their mean is 611 ms
;     8  which is a cadence of 98 steps per minute — from a sensor that told us nothing
;    16  the 15:20 walk offers only ONE interval under the 3 s gap rule
;    32  and so reports -1 rather than call one interval a rhythm
;    64  a single timestamp has no intervals at all and also reports -1
;
; The teaching: permission masked the value and left the clock alone, and the clock was
; always where the gait lived. -1 here means "too thin to call a tempo" and never "no
; movement" — two claims that must not collapse into one number.

(do
    (cadence-from-masked-steps-check))
